course: dictionary
lesson: 2965
title: Drought: when the rain stops
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A drought is a long time with little or no rain. The land gets very dry, and water becomes hard to find. «In a drought, the herd went back to a waterhole they had not visited for years.» The herd needs that water because the rain has not come for a long time.
explain: Use the words around drought to find its meaning. Words like «dry», «scarce» and «no rain» all point the same way. Ask yourself: what would the land look like? Cracked, brown and dusty. That picture is the meaning.
explain: Drought can also mean a long time without something you need or want. In football, a «goal drought» means a team has not scored for a long time. The word is the same, but the context changes its meaning, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A drought is a long period with little or no rain.
fact: During a drought, the land becomes very dry and water is scarce, which means it is hard to get.
fact: «Drought» can also mean a long time without something needed, as in «a goal drought».
fact: «Drought-resistant» plants can survive with very little water.
fact: Elephants remember distant water in droughts, and beavers' dams hold water when droughts come.
exercise: In «in a drought, the herd went back to a waterhole», what is a drought? | A journey to a new town | *A long time with little or no rain | A very wet season with floods | A kind of animal
exercise: Nadia says a «goal drought» means the team has scored too many goals. What does it really mean? | A game played in the rain | *A long time without scoring | A team that scores every minute | A goal that was scored by mistake
exercise: «A drought in 2023 forced the canal to limit the number of ships.» What did the drought force the canal to do? | Add more water to the ships | Build a new lock | *Limit the number of ships | Close for a holiday
test: «Plants that are drought-resistant can survive with very little water.» What does drought-resistant suggest? | *Able to survive with little water | Needs a lot of rain every day | Able to grow only in snow | Able to float on a river
test: Which phrase means a team has not scored for a long time? | a severe drought | a hosepipe ban | a water restriction | *a goal drought
exam: In «a severe drought left the rivers dry», what does drought mean? | *A long time with little or no rain, so rivers and land dry out | A time of heavy snow that blocks the roads | A kind of boat | A sudden loud noise
